    "done_when": "docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-reference-scope.html answers §7's two open design points, read-only, from code and cached data. First, the axis. §7 says whether PSRC's plasma centre may stand for the magnetic axis in the reference loader is settled at re-scope. Read E101011 (shot 101011) PSRC from the cache at /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/101011.zarr through §6's SELENE loader, and its G-EQDSK at /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/101011.geqdsk through imas_ambix/challenge/loader.py load_geqdsk. At the G-EQDSK's time, report PSRC's plasma centre, the G-EQDSK's magnetic axis (rmaxis, zmaxis) and the distance between them in metres. Say what PSRC's centre is: geometric or magnetic, citing the channel's EDDB description or the §6 inventory fragment jtmm-psrc-selene-inventory.html. Recommend whether the loader may pass PSRC's centre as the axis to imas_ambix/worldmodel/equilibrium_labels.py build_geometry_from_arrays, and with what flag. Second, the psi binding. Read the machine-map engine (imas_alambic's catalogue, map and transform code as installed in the project environment) and /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/maps/equilibrium.json. State whether a signal map can bind a file-backed source such as a G-EQDSK into equilibrium/time_slice/profiles_2d/psi, or whether profiles_2d psi must come through another route. Name that route, the files a binding node would write, and the COCOS 1 to 17 conversion (multiply by -2 pi) step it needs. Also say whether the open question eqdb-reader is overtaken by decision jt60sa-psi-q-source. Use one figure under docs/figures/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-reference-scope/: E101011's G-EQDSK psi contours with the PSRC boundary, the PSRC centre and the G-EQDSK axis overlaid, drawn to the repository's data-ink plot rules. Nothing is fetched over ssh, nothing under maps/ is written, and the work runs on the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set) with the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/.",
